1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,294
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:03,378 --> 00:00:05,588
<i>- Is Alvin on his way?</i>
<i>- I don't know.</i>

3
00:00:06,589 --> 00:00:09,175
<i>- Alvin isn't coming.</i>
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:10,176
<i>Oh my God!</i>

5
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,177
<i>Why?</i>

6
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:13,263
<i>I'm glad I went home.</i>

7
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:14,472
<i>Who's gonna be by your side?</i>

8
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,307
[BILLY] <i>I believe that</i>

9
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:20,770
<i>love should only</i>
<i>be given to the right person.</i>

10
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,605
<i>We're products of destiny.</i>

11
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:24,065
- [OOHING]
<i>- Yeah. </i>[CHUCKLES]

12
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:25,608
[BILLY] <i>Oliver?</i>

13
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:28,486
<i>Oliver? I'm here! Can you hear me?</i>

14
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:32,198
<i>Diabetes is really a traitor,</i>
<i>especially at Oliver's age.</i>

15
00:00:32,282 --> 00:00:36,494
<i>I feel like</i>
<i>we need to visualize LoveLine more.</i>

16
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:37,579
<i>Billy, can we talk?</i>

17
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:40,957
<i>Have you really thought this through?</i>

18
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,000
<i>I want him.</i>

19
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:45,420
[MUSIC FADES]

20
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:47,130
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

21
00:00:55,138 --> 00:01:00,226
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

22
00:01:00,894 --> 00:01:02,395
- [DOOR CREAKS]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

23
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:04,230
- Dude.
- Hmm?

24
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:06,107
- Relax.
- [FORCED CHUCKLE]

25
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:08,943
Nice. Hey, if you want,

26
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,445
I can move the furniture around.

27
00:01:10,528 --> 00:01:11,488
Huh?

28
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:13,865
- So there's more space here.
- Nope. No need.

29
00:01:13,948 --> 00:01:16,076
- [JORDAN] It's fine.
- No, that's okay. That's okay.

30
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,368
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

31
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:19,079
- That's okay. Okay.
- Sure.

32
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,330
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey.

33
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:21,372
Thank you.

34
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:24,417
You chose the bar as your venue.

35
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:25,710
You're the best.

36
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:31,090
And I heard Val is your new endorser?

37
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:33,051
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

38
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:35,845
- I'm surprised you can afford her fee.
- Huh?

39
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:37,514
- "New"?
- Are you okay?

40
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:40,975
[VALERIE] I've been endorsing it
since way back.

41
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:43,561
I keep hyping up LoveList for you

42
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:46,022
because I want
to support your best friend.

43
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,190
Thanks, babe.

44
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:51,319
[VALERIE] Let's start.

45
00:01:54,697 --> 00:01:55,698
Come with me.

46
00:01:56,324 --> 00:01:57,158
[JORDAN] Where?

47
00:01:57,784 --> 00:01:59,327
There. Stay there.

48
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:00,495
I need to check the lighting.

49
00:02:00,578 --> 00:02:01,955
It's good, right? Yes?

50
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:02,914
- All good.
- Hold on.

51
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:03,873
Why me?

52
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:04,791
Okay.

53
00:02:06,292 --> 00:02:07,335
Okay.

54
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:10,130
Dude?

55
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:18,471
I was raised by a couple
with a perfect marriage.

56
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:21,766
And I'm their only princess.

57
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:26,062
No wonder I grew up
believing that someday,

58
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,565
my Prince Charming will come and find me.

59
00:02:29,315 --> 00:02:32,360
[CAMERAS CLICKING]

60
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:36,489
Babe, there's so much more
to you than just your looks.

61
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:38,116
Wow.

62
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:40,243
You're very talented.

63
00:02:40,326 --> 00:02:43,163
You run a very successful business.

64
00:02:44,622 --> 00:02:46,958
You have a stable career here at LoveList,

65
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:49,377
and most of all,

66
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,463
I have seen how you take care
of your grandpa.

67
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,258
[CAMERAS CLICKING]

68
00:02:55,341 --> 00:02:57,343
All I'm trying to say is,

69
00:02:57,427 --> 00:03:01,681
I finally found my Prince Charming.
[GIGGLES]

70
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:03,141
[CROWD CHEERS]

71
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:08,396
Babe?

72
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:14,152
Will you marry me?

73
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:20,116
- [ROUSING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CAMERAS CLICKING]

74
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,804
Can we talk?

75
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:45,225
Just us two.

76
00:03:45,767 --> 00:03:47,769
- [STAMMERS]
- Please. Let's go.

77
00:03:47,852 --> 00:03:49,020
Come on.

78
00:03:49,103 --> 00:03:50,063
Excuse me.

79
00:03:51,314 --> 00:03:52,482
[JORDAN] Excuse me.

80
00:03:53,858 --> 00:03:55,235
[ROUSING MUSIC FADES]

81
00:03:55,318 --> 00:04:02,033
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:42,448
Val.

83
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:44,534
I'm so sorry.

84
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:46,953
I'm not ready.

85
00:04:47,036 --> 00:04:48,621
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- Huh?

86
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:51,291
You're seriously going to embarrass me?

87
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:52,959
Look, Val.

88
00:04:53,876 --> 00:04:55,962
I love you, okay?

89
00:04:56,045 --> 00:04:57,130
I'm sure of that.

90
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,800
But a wedding engagement?
I think it's just so sudden.

91
00:05:00,883 --> 00:05:02,176
"Sudden"?

92
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:04,262
What do you mean, "sudden"?

93
00:05:05,346 --> 00:05:07,974
We've been together
for almost a year, Jordan.

94
00:05:08,057 --> 00:05:11,436
Do you know how many men have tried
to court me while we've been together?

95
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:14,314
My God, I wasted a year!

96
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:15,690
"Wasted"?

97
00:05:16,774 --> 00:05:17,900
Hold on.

98
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:19,402
I didn't say yes.

99
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:21,446
But that doesn't mean we're broken up.

100
00:05:23,072 --> 00:05:24,449
I'm just not ready yet.

101
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:27,035
There's

102
00:05:27,118 --> 00:05:28,453
still so much I want to achieve.

103
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:31,873
I've got a lot of plans
for Grandpa and me.

104
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:35,126
I want to save some more. I want to--

105
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,004
If I commit to a person…

106
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:39,630
It should be with the one you really love.

107
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:42,008
[JORDAN GROANS]
Babe…

108
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:45,344
The truth is, you don't love me.

109
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:47,847
And I am not included in your plans.

110
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:51,142
Val, listen.

111
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,478
Again…

112
00:05:55,563 --> 00:05:57,523
I love you.

113
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:02,653
But not enough to say yes.

114
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:07,992
[MUSIC TURNS ROUSING]

115
00:06:24,842 --> 00:06:31,432
[ROUSING MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:46,781
Hello? Where are you?
I've been here for ages!

117
00:06:46,864 --> 00:06:48,491
Please hurry.

118
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:53,329
[SCOFFS]

119
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:55,206
You knew it all along.

120
00:06:56,791 --> 00:07:00,044
That's why you asked me
if I was sure of my decision.

121
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:03,631
- Because you knew he was gonna say no!
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:07,218
Val. Don't drag Billy into this.

123
00:07:07,301 --> 00:07:08,177
[VALERIE] Why not?

124
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:12,390
She's the reason I proposed to you.

125
00:07:12,473 --> 00:07:17,061
Because I can see and I can feel
that you deem her more important than me!

126
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:19,313
Val, that's not true.

127
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:22,108
Jordan and I are just friends.

128
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:23,693
Seriously, Billy?

129
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,863
With the way you guys look at each other?

130
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,990
With how you hug each other so tightly?

131
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:34,245
And did you notice that
every time we're together,

132
00:07:34,328 --> 00:07:37,874
even for your tiniest problems,
he runs off like it's life and death!

133
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,417
[JORDAN] Val.

134
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,128
Oliver being hospitalized
wasn't a small problem.

135
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:44,422
They're my family.

136
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:47,967
All my blood relatives are gone.

137
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:50,094
Dad left. Mom's dead.

138
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:51,929
Grandpa Jude is sick.

139
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:55,183
Billy and her family are

140
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:56,767
all I have left.

141
00:07:56,851 --> 00:07:58,561
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

142
00:07:58,644 --> 00:07:59,812
[SCOFFS]

143
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:02,773
So it really is Billy, huh?

144
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:05,234
[SIGHS]

145
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:08,154
Well, Billy, I hope you're happy now!

146
00:08:08,237 --> 00:08:09,155
[SNIFFLES]

147
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,656
You finally have Jordan all to yourself!

148
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,283
But you guess what?

149
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:13,951
Karma's a bitch, you know.

150
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:16,287
- And it's coming for you.
- [HORN HONKING]

151
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,539
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

152
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,875
[CAR DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

153
00:08:35,973 --> 00:08:40,686
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:47,193
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

155
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,544
[BLAIRE] My goodness, chief.

156
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:08,130
Should we report this to
the cops so it gets on record?

157
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:09,257
Or do we take revenge?

158
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:10,967
I've got cousins who are robbers.

159
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,051
[CHARM] Are you sure?

160
00:09:12,134 --> 00:09:14,136
It might only add fuel to the fire.

161
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,179
[RALPH] Well, Billy, if you want,

162
00:09:15,263 --> 00:09:17,265
I know someone who works on car detailing.

163
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,558
Leave it to me.

164
00:09:18,641 --> 00:09:21,060
No, I'll handle it.
Rubbing compound can solve this.

165
00:09:21,143 --> 00:09:23,104
But it'll take about an hour.

166
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:27,608
You know, it should be Valerie
who fixes and pays for that.

167
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:30,319
What she did was wrong.
That's so immature!

168
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,905
Billy, why aren't you saying anything?

169
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,909
Do you have CCTV in the area?

170
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:39,036
- Yes.
- Why?

171
00:09:40,788 --> 00:09:43,374
Because it seems impossible
for Valerie to have done this.

172
00:09:43,457 --> 00:09:45,876
When she went out,
I followed her right away.

173
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:49,547
Ma'am, I'm sorry.
I already checked the CCTV.

174
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:53,593
This is a blind spot,
so the camera couldn't catch it.

175
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:57,597
Well, I'm sure Valerie did this!

176
00:10:06,439 --> 00:10:13,404
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

177
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:34,342
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:48,856
I miss you, Grandpa.

179
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:51,525
I miss the old days.

180
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,155
Whenever I had a problem,

181
00:10:57,281 --> 00:10:58,783
I'd always go to your room

182
00:11:00,618 --> 00:11:01,911
and stay by your side.

183
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:04,163
I'd tell you stories

184
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:05,915
until the sun comes up.

185
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:08,334
- [SNORES]
- [SIGHS]

186
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:11,295
I wish things were still that easy.

187
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,006
Simple.

188
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:18,594
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,012
[INHALES SHARPLY]

190
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:22,848
Grandpa!

191
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:24,767
Who are you?

192
00:11:25,601 --> 00:11:27,603
My name is Jordan. I'm your grandson.

193
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,897
Here. This is our picture.

194
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:31,816
You don't look like my grandson.

195
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:33,317
I am your grandson.

196
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,903
- [JUDE] If you don't leave, I'll scream.
- Grandpa, please.

197
00:11:35,986 --> 00:11:38,489
Calm down, Grandpa. It's me, Jordan.

198
00:11:38,572 --> 00:11:40,157
- Thief!
- Grandpa?

199
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:41,867
- Thief!
- Okay, fine!

200
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,160
- Thief!
- Please, calm down.

201
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:45,538
- I'm leaving.
- T-thief!

202
00:11:45,621 --> 00:11:46,789
I love you, Grandpa.

203
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:53,629
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:57,508
I knew you'd go here.

205
00:12:05,891 --> 00:12:06,725
Sorry.

206
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:11,439
[JORDAN CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

207
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:12,940
You set me up, dude.

208
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:16,569
[SIGHS] I didn't know what to do.

209
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:20,030
I felt it wasn't my place to stop Val

210
00:12:20,114 --> 00:12:21,866
because, of course, it's her relationship.

211
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,784
I didn't want to meddle.

212
00:12:23,868 --> 00:12:25,911
But you know my plans, right?

213
00:12:25,995 --> 00:12:27,621
We even talked about it, didn't we?

214
00:12:27,705 --> 00:12:29,540
I know. I'm sorry!

215
00:12:29,623 --> 00:12:32,751
You didn't even warn me.
You could've at least given me a heads-up.

216
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,837
It was wrong, okay? It was wrong.

217
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:37,047
Don't I dislike people who deceive others?

218
00:12:37,131 --> 00:12:38,883
And then I kept a secret from you?

219
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:41,218
What kind of a friend is that?

220
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:43,137
Wrong. It was really wrong.

221
00:12:43,762 --> 00:12:44,930
[SIGHS]

222
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,849
Again, I'm sorry.

223
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:49,602
I'm sorry too.

224
00:12:50,644 --> 00:12:52,396
You even got dragged into this mess.

225
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,816
[SIGHS] Don't worry about it.

226
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:58,152
Yani and Ralph said
they'll take care of it.

227
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:01,530
What's that?

228
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:02,865
Hey, stop it!

229
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:04,158
Stop, Jordan.

230
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:06,660
Val shouldn't have done that.

231
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:09,455
We're not even sure yet if Val did it.

232
00:13:09,538 --> 00:13:11,040
The CCTV didn't capture anything.

233
00:13:11,123 --> 00:13:12,791
Don't call.

234
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:19,465
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

235
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,426
Tomorrow is…

236
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,637
- Mm.
- Mm-hmm.

237
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:28,432
It's the death anniversary of our mothers.

238
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:37,233
[JUDE] <i>Why did you punch him?</i>
<i>You should've let it go.</i>

239
00:13:37,316 --> 00:13:38,776
<i>They were teasing me.</i>

240
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:42,029
<i>They said I'd fail to get</i>
<i>into computer engineering.</i>

241
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:43,864
[JUDE] <i>Once your mother</i>
<i>finds out about this,</i>

242
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:45,032
<i>she will be furious again.</i>

243
00:13:45,115 --> 00:13:46,825
<i>Well, I have a peace offering.</i>

244
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:50,496
<i>Wow, you even have a bribe.</i>

245
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:52,331
[LAUGHING]

246
00:13:52,414 --> 00:13:53,958
<i>Look at this kid.</i>

247
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:56,335
[CHUCKLES]

248
00:13:56,418 --> 00:14:01,173
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

249
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:02,883
<i>Jade?</i>

250
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:05,803
<i>Jade!</i>

251
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:07,054
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Mommy!</i>

252
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:08,264
<i>Mommy!</i>

253
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:10,558
[CRYING] <i>Mommy!</i>

254
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:15,020
[SNIFFLES] <i>Mommy…</i>

255
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,647
[CRYING CONTINUES]

256
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:18,023
<i>Help.</i>

257
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,233
<i>Help!</i>

258
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:21,443
<i>Anyone! Help us!</i>

259
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:23,904
[YOUNG JORDAN CRYING] <i>Mommy!</i>

260
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:26,282
<i>We still haven't identified</i>

261
00:14:26,949 --> 00:14:29,535
<i>who crashed into your daughter, sir.</i>

262
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:32,037
<i>No one saw the car's license plate.</i>

263
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:34,290
<i>There's no video surveillance</i>
<i>in the area either.</i>

264
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:36,959
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>Will you just</i>
<i>keep telling us that again?</i>

265
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:38,878
<i>Is that it already?</i>

266
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:40,880
<i>Isn't there anything else we can do?</i>

267
00:14:40,963 --> 00:14:43,465
[INVESTIGATOR] <i>The autopsy report</i>
<i>hasn't been released yet.</i>

268
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:46,010
<i>That's why we have nothing</i>
<i>to tell you as of now.</i>

269
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:48,470
[SOBS] <i>Is that everything you can do?</i>

270
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:50,806
- [CRYING]
- [CHAIR SCRAPES]

271
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,767
<i>We've come here over and over again!</i>

272
00:14:53,851 --> 00:14:54,977
[JUDE] <i>Jordan, dear…</i>

273
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:56,562
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>No, Grandpa.</i>

274
00:14:56,645 --> 00:14:57,521
[JUDE] <i>That's enough.</i>

275
00:14:57,605 --> 00:14:58,689
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>No, Grandpa!</i>

276
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:00,524
<i>- That's my mother!</i>
<i>- Enough. That's enough.</i>

277
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,234
[YOUNG JORDAN] <i>That's not enough!</i>

278
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,320
<i>That's my mother!</i>

279
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,530
<i>- Let's go.</i>
- [SOBBING]

280
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:07,489
<i>No!</i>

281
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,241
[JUDE] <i>Jordan.</i>

282
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:11,160
[SOBBING CONTINUES]

283
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:13,537
<i>- Hush now.</i>
- [SOBBING, WHIMPERING]

284
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:15,998
[YOUNG JORDAN KEEPS SOBBING]

285
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:22,796
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

286
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:28,928
I went to the police station earlier.

287
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:32,306
It's been years.

288
00:15:32,389 --> 00:15:34,975
There is still no update
about my mom's case.

289
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:39,813
Our justice system here works really slow.

290
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:44,985
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

291
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:49,365
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

292
00:15:49,448 --> 00:15:51,492
[JORDAN] As long as I'm alive,

293
00:15:51,575 --> 00:15:53,077
I won't stop

294
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,079
until there's justice for you, Mom.

295
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:57,081
I won't stop

296
00:15:57,915 --> 00:16:00,376
until the person who hit you
gets arrested.

297
00:16:01,251 --> 00:16:02,294
I promise.

298
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:11,679
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

299
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:12,972
[OLIVER] Bro Dude!

300
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:21,271
[MUSIC TURNS GENTLE]

301
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:24,441
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday to you! ♪</i>
- To me!

302
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:28,529
<i>♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday ♪</i>

303
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:32,324
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

304
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:33,701
To me!

305
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:37,037
- [PRECIOUS] There you go.
- Yay! Happy birthday!

306
00:16:37,121 --> 00:16:38,872
- Thank you.
- Yahoo!

307
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:39,915
[OLIVER] Thank you.

308
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,127
To Mother

309
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:45,337
and to Father.

310
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:48,882
Do you know what my birthday wish is?

311
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,050
What?

312
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:54,054
I wish we could visit
Papa's grave in America.

313
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:57,891
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

314
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:58,851
Mm.

315
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:02,813
Oh, here you go! Open this.

316
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:04,189
Here.

317
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:05,858
- Birthday gift?
- Yes!

318
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:07,276
Thank you, Billy!

319
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:09,278
- [GIFT WRAP CRUMPLING]
- Wow.

320
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:10,738
That's what you wanted, right?

321
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:12,072
It's also blue!

322
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:14,033
- Headphones!
- Yes!

323
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:15,409
- Thank you, Billy!
- [JORDAN] Wow.

324
00:17:15,492 --> 00:17:17,453
- That's your favorite color!
- [OLIVER] Blue!

325
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:19,455
- This one's from Auntie.
- Okay then.

326
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:21,498
- That's from Auntie.
- That's stylish.

327
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,542
Wow, how competitive.

328
00:17:23,625 --> 00:17:24,626
[ADMIRING GASPS]

329
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,462
- I think that's my size.
- Wow, T-shirt!

330
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:27,963
- It's nice!
- Hmm!

331
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,548
It's nice! Thank you, Auntie.

332
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:31,925
- Thank you, Auntie.
- Okay, sure, sure.

333
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:33,886
Of course, Bro Dude got you a gift too.

334
00:17:33,969 --> 00:17:34,803
Okay.

335
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:38,182
Bro Dude?!

336
00:17:39,349 --> 00:17:42,061
- [JORDAN] Oh?
- I've wanted this for so long! Thank you!

337
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:43,437
[BILLY] Oh…?

338
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:45,522
- Thank you!
- You see that?

339
00:17:45,606 --> 00:17:48,400
- Oh, he gets a hug, huh.
- You're welcome, little dude.

340
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:51,445
By the way, Auntie Pres,
go ahead to the foundation first later.

341
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:52,362
Okay.

342
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:55,365
I just need to pick up a check,
then I'll catch up with you.

343
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,076
- All right. Okay, let's eat.
- Okay.

344
00:17:57,159 --> 00:17:58,327
- Okay!
- Let me fix this first.

345
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,704
Hey, pay attention to our gift too!

346
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:03,832
- Oh, here it is.
- Unbelievable!

347
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,918
- [JORDAN] Happy birthday.
- [OLIVER] Thank you.

348
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,544
[BILLY] Let's eat, everyone.

349
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,421
- Let's eat!
- Let's eat!

350
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:16,053
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

351
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:17,429
What's wrong?

352
00:18:17,513 --> 00:18:19,098
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

353
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:20,474
Nothing.

354
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:22,309
I just feel like someone's watching me.

355
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,647
Oh my! That could be…

356
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:28,315
the one for you.

357
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:29,775
- [PRECIOUS SQUEALS]
- [LIGHT SMACK]

358
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:31,026
- [CHUCKLING]
- Oliver saw that.

359
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,027
[BILLY] Sorry!

360
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:34,113
[BILLY] Separate them. Let's eat.

361
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:35,989
Hello, Ma'am Billy!

362
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:37,950
- Good afternoon.
- Good afternoon, ma'am.

363
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:40,369
- Hi, Tina! Where's Auntie Pres?
- Hello, Ma'am Billy.

364
00:18:40,452 --> 00:18:41,745
- She's inside?
- Yes, ma'am.

365
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,877
- Hi, Auntie!
- Billy, hi!

366
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:52,381
Hang on, I'm busy right now.
I'm just talking to someone.

367
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:54,091
- But Precious is there.
- All right.

368
00:18:54,174 --> 00:18:55,551
I'm just talking to someone.

369
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:03,016
All of us here believe you'll get through
everything you're going through.

370
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,561
If they made it through, so can you.

371
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:10,691
[BILLY] Auntie Pres.

372
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,234
I got it.

373
00:19:12,317 --> 00:19:15,445
I'll catch up with you, okay?
Go ahead first.

374
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:18,157
- [PRECIOUS] Wow!
- I got it!

375
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:22,119
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

376
00:19:22,744 --> 00:19:24,538
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

377
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:29,209
We have a new donation from LoveList!

378
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,419
[CHUCKLING]

379
00:19:30,502 --> 00:19:32,629
- [APPLAUDING]
- It's from LoveList.

380
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:35,048
- [APPLAUDING]
- Yes.

381
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:38,468
[CHUCKLING]

382
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:41,972
What you brought is so delicious.

383
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:45,893
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

384
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:47,060
I think…

385
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:51,565
this is my daughter's favorite.

386
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:54,109
That's right.

387
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,111
Jade said

388
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,363
you should eat well.

389
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:00,949
She also said to take your meds on time

390
00:20:01,783 --> 00:20:03,702
so you'll get stronger.

391
00:20:03,785 --> 00:20:04,912
[SIGHS]

392
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:06,788
What else did she say?

393
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,333
She loves you very much.

394
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:14,546
I love her very much too.

395
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:15,797
[SOBS SOFTLY]

396
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:17,007
Tell her…

397
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:18,800
[EXHALES]

398
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:20,886
…to come visit me sometime.

399
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:24,056
- Okay.
- [SOBS SOFTLY]

400
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:27,100
I miss her so much.

401
00:20:27,184 --> 00:20:28,685
[SNIFFLES]

402
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:30,646
Me too.

403
00:20:31,688 --> 00:20:32,773
What?

404
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:33,982
Wait a second.

405
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:37,194
Who are you?

406
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:39,404
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

407
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:40,781
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

408
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:44,618
[NURSE] Time to take
your medicine, Grandpa Jude.

409
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,870
Sir Jordan, we'll get going now.

410
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:48,622
Okay, let's go.

411
00:20:48,705 --> 00:20:50,916
- Careful.
- Take care, Grandpa.

412
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,292
I love you.

413
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:58,298
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

414
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:00,926
Yes, Nurse Marie.

415
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:04,096
About Grandpa's expenses… I'm sorry.

416
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:07,975
If only I could bring him home.

417
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:09,601
But…

418
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:11,937
I'm afraid he'd just run away again.

419
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:16,650
I also can't afford
to hire a nurse right now.

420
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:17,818
[JORDAN SIGHS]

421
00:21:17,901 --> 00:21:20,445
I hope you never get tired of
taking care of your grandpa.

422
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:23,198
[CHUCKLES] Oh, that'll never happen.

423
00:21:24,324 --> 00:21:25,742
[JORDAN] I owe him my life.

424
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:28,287
He's the only family I have left.

425
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:31,707
I'll never forget him. Never.

426
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:34,751
[PATS SHOULDER]

427
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:38,255
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

428
00:21:38,338 --> 00:21:41,008
[BILLY] This is called art therapy.

429
00:21:41,091 --> 00:21:44,636
Through this, you'll be able
to express yourself freely.

430
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,221
There's no right or wrong,

431
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:49,599
so just let out whatever's in your hearts.

432
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,484
Why are you painting a bird?

433
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:02,446
[ABI] Because I want to be free.

434
00:22:03,613 --> 00:22:05,198
Free from what?

435
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:07,659
From life.

436
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:12,122
I feel like I'm trapped.

437
00:22:12,205 --> 00:22:14,333
Trapped by what?

438
00:22:18,837 --> 00:22:20,547
Trapped by…

439
00:22:21,381 --> 00:22:24,426
By taking care of my sick mother.

440
00:22:25,135 --> 00:22:27,137
My father left us.

441
00:22:28,346 --> 00:22:30,182
So did my sibling.

442
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:33,101
So…

443
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:38,774
I've been taking care of
my sick mother all by myself.

444
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:45,405
I love my mom, but…

445
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:48,075
[SNIFFLES]

446
00:22:48,158 --> 00:22:52,079
…sometimes, you know,
it just gets exhausting.

447
00:22:52,162 --> 00:22:54,873
[SOBS] It's exhausting because

448
00:22:54,956 --> 00:22:56,917
it feels like I've given
everything to everyone,

449
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,919
and there's nothing left for myself.

450
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:03,215
[SNIFFLES]

451
00:23:06,134 --> 00:23:07,302
[SOBS]

452
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:09,554
Did she do that to you?

453
00:23:09,638 --> 00:23:10,722
[SNIFFLES]

454
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:17,729
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

455
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:22,651
You know, you can talk to her now.

456
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:26,530
If you want, we can go with you.

457
00:23:26,613 --> 00:23:29,449
Tell her how you really feel.

458
00:23:29,533 --> 00:23:30,784
Oh, no.

459
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,619
Thanks, but no.

460
00:23:32,702 --> 00:23:33,703
I'm okay here.

461
00:23:33,787 --> 00:23:38,959
Just having something to do,
having people to talk to,

462
00:23:39,042 --> 00:23:41,336
having people looking out for me,

463
00:23:41,419 --> 00:23:42,796
that's more than enough.

464
00:23:42,879 --> 00:23:44,131
Thank you.

465
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:49,719
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

466
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:51,680
By the way, I'm Billy.

467
00:23:54,266 --> 00:24:00,313
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

468
00:24:03,483 --> 00:24:04,651
Of course.

469
00:24:05,610 --> 00:24:07,195
Benilda Cariño.

470
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:10,157
I know who you are.
I've been following you.

471
00:24:10,782 --> 00:24:12,993
I'm a huge fan of LoveList.

472
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:14,411
- Mmm.
- I know everything about you.

473
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:16,204
Even what happened
between you and your fiancé.

474
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:18,373
- Mm-hmm.
- But that was a long time ago.

475
00:24:18,456 --> 00:24:20,167
Oh. Sorry, sorry.

476
00:24:20,250 --> 00:24:22,502
I'm just a big LoveList fan.

477
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:24,880
- That's why I know so much about you.
- Thank you.

478
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,339
Um…

479
00:24:26,423 --> 00:24:27,257
I'm Abi.

480
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:29,342
Abi Mercado.

481
00:24:29,426 --> 00:24:30,802
Abi.

482
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:31,845
Uh…

483
00:24:32,512 --> 00:24:33,889
Miss Benilda?

484
00:24:34,431 --> 00:24:36,266
Can I ask you a favor?

485
00:24:37,058 --> 00:24:38,476
Of course. What is it?

486
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:42,355
Can I get a hug from my idol?

487
00:24:43,106 --> 00:24:44,482
Of course.

488
00:24:45,650 --> 00:24:47,027
[ABI SQUEALING]

489
00:24:47,110 --> 00:24:48,028
[GIGGLES SOFTLY]

490
00:24:51,072 --> 00:24:57,954
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

491
00:25:02,042 --> 00:25:04,836
[PRECIOUS] So she's a fan of yours too?

492
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:08,548
You know, Abigail Mercado
has quite a story.

493
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:09,966
- Mm-hmm.
- Yeah.

494
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:12,093
I keep thinking,

495
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:14,721
she's had it pretty rough too, hasn't she?

496
00:25:15,305 --> 00:25:18,350
I mean, if it's a boyfriend or a husband,

497
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:19,726
you can leave.

498
00:25:20,435 --> 00:25:22,604
But when it's your parents…

499
00:25:23,647 --> 00:25:27,943
And on top of that,
her father and her sibling abandoned her.

500
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:30,946
Well, you can relate, can't you?

501
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:34,241
Good thing someone recommended

502
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:36,451
Angels of Grace to her, Auntie Precious.

503
00:25:36,534 --> 00:25:40,914
And you know,
I heard she's a college graduate.

504
00:25:40,997 --> 00:25:43,500
- Oh!
- Maybe she focused on

505
00:25:43,583 --> 00:25:46,920
taking care of her mom,
so she never got the chance

506
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:49,631
to build a career of her own.

507
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:51,258
What did she major in?

508
00:25:51,341 --> 00:25:52,968
Marketing?

509
00:25:53,051 --> 00:25:56,429
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

510
00:26:00,058 --> 00:26:04,145
[BILLY] <i>And because we are celebrating</i>
<i>our second anniversary,</i>

511
00:26:04,229 --> 00:26:09,901
<i>we are preparing something</i>
<i>bigger and better for LoveList.</i>

512
